rfile expects a SPARQL query that enumerates all the artifacts that need to be downloaded and imported.
Following query was used for current instance:

PREFIX dataid: <http://dataid.dbpedia.org/ns/core#>
 PREFIX dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
 PREFIX dcat: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#>
 SELECT ?file {
 {
 ?dataset dataid:artifact ?artifact . ?dataset dataid:version ?latest . ?dataset dcat:distribution ?distribution. ?distribution dataid:contentVariant 'en'^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> . ?distribution dcat:downloadURL ?file . {
 SELECT ?artifact (max(?version) as ?latest) WHERE {
 ?dataset dataid:group ?group . FILTER (?group in (<https://databus.dbpedia.org/dbpedia/generic>, <https://databus.dbpedia.org/dbpedia/generic>, <https://databus.dbpedia.org/dbpedia/mappings> )) . ?dataset dataid:artifact ?artifact . FILTER (?artifact != <https://databus.dbpedia.org/dbpedia/generic/wikilinks>)
 ?dataset dataid:version ?version .

?dataset dataid:artifact ?artifact . FILTER (?artifact != <https://databus.dbpedia.org/dbpedia/generic/wikilinks>)
 ?dataset dataid:version ?version .

?dataset dataid:artifact ?artifact . FILTER (?artifact != <https://databus.dbpedia.org/dbpedia/generic/wikilinks>)
 ?dataset dataid:version ?version . } GROUP BY ?artifact order by desc (?artifact)
 }
 } UNION {
 ?dataset dataid:artifact <https://databus.dbpedia.org/dbpedia/ontology/dbo-snapshots> . ?dataset dcat:distribution ?distribution . ?distribution dcat:downloadURL ?file . } 
 } order by desc(?file)

This query gets all the latest DBpedia artifacts for English language.

